OK, I'm officially an exlojbanist. I attempted to learn the words before realizing that they were more irregular than even English!  Rafsi are basically conjugations, and they have no discernable pattern, other than being composed of letters from the gismu.  Modals are directly related to gismu, and many are irregular.  The grammar is still very interesting, though.  Now I describe lojban to the outside world as having logical grammar, hexadecimal numbers, and rampant irregularities.

